Since 1944 Tuva has been part of the RSFSR, then the Russian Federation.

==Threshold of originality== <!--T:54-->

</translate>
<noinclude>{{CRT shortcut|TOO|Russia}}</noinclude>
<translate>
===Automatic camera works=== <!--T:62-->

<!--T:55-->
[[File:PD-icon.svg|25px|link=|Public domain]] use {{tlx|PD-RU-exempt-autocam}}

<!--T:58-->
{{okMark}} A photowork or a videowork made by '''automatic''' camera (Russian: ''автоматическая камера'', not to be confused with automated camera: ''автоматизированная камера'') is not the subject of copyright, because such work is made by technical tool without creative human activity.<ref>The Supreme Court of the Russian Federation, Part 80 of Session Resolution No. 10 of April 23, 2019 on Application of Part IV of the Civil Code of the Russian Federation</ref>

<!--T:56-->
'''Examples'''
* Any photowork or videowork made by '''automatic''' camera for administrative violation record (for example, by '''automatic''' camera for driving offense record<ref name=FineCamera/>).<ref>The Supreme Court of the Russian Federation, Part 80 of Session Resolution No. 10 of April 23, 2019 on Application of Part IV of the Civil Code of the Russian Federation</ref>

===Simple creative works=== <!--T:63-->

<!--T:60-->
{{NotMark}} Simple result of creative work (creative human activity) is copyrightable.<ref>The Supreme Court of the Russian Federation, Part 80 of Session Resolution No. 10 of April 23, 2019 on Application of Part IV of the Civil Code of the Russian Federation</ref>

<!--T:61-->
'''Examples'''
* Simple black square as geometric shape is uncopyrightable as itself. However [[:Category:Black Square (Malevich)|''Black Square'']] by ''Kazimir Malevich'' was copyrightable because this painting was the result of creative work in recognized art style - ''[[:en:suprematism|suprematism]]'', and it is in Public Domain because of copyright term expiry, not because of result simplicity.

===Logos=== <!--T:64-->

<!--T:65-->
{{neutral|In doubt}} There is no clear precedent in Russian courts for the threshold of originality for simple logos. Presumably, simple logo, which is part of [[:en:Corporate identity|corporate identity]] stated in brandbook (brand/visual guidelines or other similar corporate document), can be considered as copyrightable part of respective creative work.

==Signatures== <!--T:68-->

</translate>
<noinclude>{{CRT shortcut|SIG|Russia}}</noinclude>
<translate>
<!--T:69-->
{{OkMark}}. Signature used for expression of will, for identification, or in similar cases is a legal or technical tool, it is not work of science, literature, or art, so it is not copyrightable.<br>
{{neutral|Depend on case}}. Signature used for other purposes can be protected depending on its creativity.

